  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that SureCN26387 may be a target of SNB-78 through multiple indirect pathways. The first pathway links SureCN26387 to Hepatocyte, which is targeted by 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One, which in turn targets SNB-78. The second pathway connects SureCN26387 to Hepatocyte, which is also targeted by Cocosamide B, which targets SNB-78. The third pathway links SureCN26387 to Raji, which is targeted by Maplexin A, which targets SNB-78. These pathways collectively suggest that SureCN26387 may interact with SNB-78 through different molecular mechanisms, possibly involving cellular targets that are modulated by various compounds. The evidence supports a potential relationship between SureCN26387 and SNB-78, but the exact mechanism of interaction remains unclear, as the pathways do not specify the direct interaction between SureCN26387 and SNB-78. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the relationship, emphasizing the need for further investigation into the molecular interactions between these entities.",
